{"availability":"available","full":"MorrisGlr/algo-art-lep-scales","name":"algo-art-lep-scales","description":"Produces a 3D animation of butterfly and moth wing scales in a web brower using Three.js. Link to in-browser demo provided.","category":"Design","language":"JavaScript","stars":1,"forks":0,"created":"2025-05-19T18:08:47Z","updated":"2026-05-11T23:13:29Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://morrisglr.github.io/algo-art-lep-scales/","topics":["algorithmic-art","animation","biology","creative-coding","entomology","generative-art","github-pages","glsl","html","interactive-art","iridescence","javascript","lepidoptera","procedural-generation","shader","structural-coloration","three-js","threejs","webgl"],"demo":"https://morrisglr.github.io/algo-art-lep-scales/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T16:07:29.030Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T16:07:29.030Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T16:07:29.030Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T16:07:29.030Z","stars":1,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Three.js"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["An algorithmic visualization of butterfly and moth wing microstructure, rendered in real-time with Three.js. 4,500 individually modeled scales oscillate in a standing wave, with structural coloration and iridescence modeled through custom GLSL shaders.","Inspired by the observation that lepidopteran scales — usually invisible to the naked eye — collectively produce the appearance of fluid motion, much like pixels resolving into image at distance.","Morris Aguilar, M.D./Ph.D., has work that spans clinical AI and computational biology. This project is part of the Computational Art History series, which translates biological and artistic structures into parametric browser-based systems."],"features":["Wing Scale — lepidopteran wing microstructure → animated scale grid (this piece)","algo-art-hopper — Edward Hopper's window compositions → Three.js parallax scene","algo-art-klint-kandinsky — Hilma af Kl